.TH "VMPK" "1" "November 6, 2026" "VMPK 0.9.3" "Virtual MIDI Piano Keyboard"
.SH NAME
\f[B]vmpk\f[R] \- Virtual MIDI Piano Keyboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]vmpk\f[R] [options...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the \f[B]vmpk\f[R] program.
.PP
This program uses standard Qt options.
.PP
Virtual MIDI Piano Keyboard is a MIDI events generator and receiver.
It doesnt produce any sound by itself, but can be used to drive a MIDI
synthesizer (either hardware or software, internal or external).
You can use the computers keyboard to play MIDI notes, and also the
mouse.
You can use the Virtual MIDI Piano Keyboard to display the played MIDI
notes from another instrument or MIDI file player.
.SH VMPK OPTIONS
The following options apply to \f[B]vmpk\f[R] only:
.PP
\f[B]\-h|\-\-help\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Displays a help text.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-v|\-\-version\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Displays version information.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-p|\-\-portable\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Enables portable settings mode using a default configuration file name.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-f\f[R] \f[I]path/file.conf\f[R]
.RS
.PP
This option implies \f[B]\-\-portable\f[R] as well.
Reads and writes \f[I]path/file.conf\f[R] as the portable settings
configuration file name.
.PP
This configuration file is always a text file with INI format, despite
the running Operating System conventions.
.RE
.SH STANDARD OPTIONS
